Import the C function fputs taking a pointer to character and a pointer to void, returning an integer, from the header "stdio.h".
Import the C function fopen taking a pointer to character and a pointer to character, returning a pointer to void, from the header "stdio.h".
Import the C function fprintf taking a pointer to void and a pointer to character and variadic parameters, returning an integer, from the header "stdio.h".
Import the C function fclose taking a pointer to void, returning an integer, from the header "stdio.h".
Import the C function fgets taking a pointer to character and an integer and a pointer to void, returning a pointer to character, from the header "stdio.h".
Import the C function remove taking a pointer to character, returning an integer, from the header "stdio.h".
Declare out as pointer to void with value Call fopen with "/tmp/plainspeak_io.txt", "w" done.
